flowchart LR
    accTitle: How chat state is stored and how it is turned back into messages
    accDescr: Chat state is an append-only event log keyed by tenant and thread, never a mutable message array. Every user message, assistant reply, tool result and steering message is appended; nothing is edited in place. What the model sees is produced at read time by a session strategy named in spec.session.strategy, and swapping the strategy changes only the render, never the log. Fork and rewind write new branches rather than deleting events, which is what makes them safe. A memory:// database URL swaps the Postgres store for an in-memory twin with the same contract, and the conformance suite runs both arms against one set of assertions.

    turn([Turn produces events]) -->|"append-only, never edits"| log[("session_events<br/>tenant_id, thread_id, seq")]

    log -->|"fork writes a new branch"| tree["Branch tree<br/>session/tree.py"]
    log -->|"rewind moves the leaf pointer"| tree
    tree -->|"names the active leaf"| state[("thread_state<br/>leaf, pin, thinking level")]

    log --> strat{"spec.session.strategy"}
    strat -->|"full_replay"| replay["Every event, in order"]
    strat -->|"windowed:N"| win["Last N turns"]
    strat -->|"compacting or summarizing:N"| comp["Summarise older turns,<br/>keep the last N"]
    strat -->|"semantic:N"| sem["Top N by relevance<br/>to the current turn"]

    replay --> msgs(["Messages handed to the model"])
    win --> msgs
    comp --> msgs
    sem --> msgs

    class log focal
    class strat focal
    class turn,msgs external
    class tree,replay,win,comp,sem primary
    class state store

